<title>USA: Columbia says 90 mmcfd U.S. Gulf gas cut.</title>
<headline>Columbia says 90 mmcfd U.S. Gulf gas cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Columbia Gulf Transmission, a unit of Columbia Gas System, said Thursday producers shut in about 90 million cubic feet per day (mmcfd) of U.S. Gulf natural gas production due to tropical storm Danny.</p>
<p>&quot;To date, the estimate is that producers have shut in about 90 mmcfd on our system,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
</text>
